This example shows how to use invisible applet/agent for pushing text into the browser
(push channel) using LJMS broker and JSObject from the server which can be used as
an idea for building of more complex conferencing tools (broadcasters).

To run it:
1.cd to the example directory and start runServer.sh under Unix or runServer.bat under Win
on the same machine where you have a web-server;
2.put the following 3 files under the web-server (htdocs for Apache):
text_frames.html, text_index.html and agent.jar
3.Open a browser (or multiple instances) against text_frames.html
4.Type something into the console (on the server) and press Enter at the end. Text you have typed should appear
in all browsers instances (having an applet - agent being connected). You can type directly
into the browser.
